.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1143 AM PDT Sun Aug 30 2026

Widespread VFR with clear skies prevails this afternoon as moderate
onshore winds increase. The marine layer was about 200 feet deeper
this morning compared to yesterday (1400 ft to 1600 ft) and will
continue to deepen tonight, resulting in MVFR ceilings at most
terminals. Low confidence on whether stratus will reach the interior
East and South Bay valley terminals, therefore the TAF hints at the
potential with SCT decks. Coastal sites develop low-end MVFR
ceilings around sunset, meanwhile the rest of the sites develop MVFR
ceilings overnight. Stratus should recede to the coast by late
Monday morning. Overall, medium confidence on the exact arrival of
stratus.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR prevails this afternoon with moderate westerly
breezes. Decreased potential for strong gusts this afternoon, though
cannot fully rule out an occasional 20 kt gust. As winds ease
overnight, MVFR stratus is expected to develop at both SFO and OAK
which then persist until late Monday morning as moderate winds
increase.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Northwest to west winds prevail through the
TAF period. VFR conditions this afternoon with medium confidence for
MVFR ceilings to develop right before sunset, though they may arrive
as late as 9 PM PDT tonight. Stratus persists overnight with the
potential for coastal drizzle early Monday morning. If coastal
drizzle occurs, anticipate a reduction to visibility around 4-6SM.

